# Cinder Glade: "This land enters tapped unless you control two or more basic lands." Turn 5 Bot1 controls a Mountain (one
# basic) and a Taiga (the Mountain and Forest types, but not basic, CR 205.4c): one basic is below the two, so its Cinder
# Glade enters tapped - though Bot2, its opponent, controls two basic lands by then. Bot2 with a Mountain and a Forest of
# its own plays the same land on turn 6 and it enters untapped (positive control).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Taiga
Cinder Glade
Forest x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Forest
Cinder Glade
Forest x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Taiga.Play
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Cinder Glade.Play
[T6 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Cinder Glade.Play

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Cinder Glade.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield.Cinder Glade.Tapped = false
